{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":1},"runs":[{"text":"Architecture","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"rc-git is layered, each layer with one job. Data moves up as immutable values keyed by object id; nothing moves down except requests.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"code","language":null,"text":"RcGitApp          AppKit views. Forward clicks to the model, render its callbacks.\u000aRcGitKit          BrowserModel (state, generations, cache), LayoutPolicy, value types.\u000arc-git-ffi        C ABI. Marshals values across; owns nothing after the call returns.\u000a  rc-git-guard      Mutation policy and the one write and network path. Reads through core.\u000a  rc-git-highlight  tree-sitter highlight spans and import links. Pure.\u000a  rc-git-core       gix wrapper. Repository pool, refs, trees, blobs, log, revision parsing,\u000a                    diff, blame, worktree status, stash listing.\u000arc-git-cli        Beside the Swift package, on core, guard and highlight."},"runs":[],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"rc-git-cli","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" sits beside the Swift package on top of the core, the guard and the highlighter, and gives scripts and agents the app's reads, its guarded mutations and its highlight and import-link passes. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rc-git-guard","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" holds the mutation policy and, in its ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"actions","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" module, the one write and network path: every mutation — refs, objects, the index, working-tree files, the stash, checkout, and fetch, pull and push — goes through it; ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"safety.md","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" has the rules. Its actions are branch and tag create and delete, commit, the stash lifecycle (push, apply, pop, drop), discard of files or hunks, the branch switch, fetch, fast-forward pull, and push; sync is those last three run in sequence by the app, not an action of its own. Network I/O exists only in the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"actions::remote","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" module; ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"safety.md","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", \"Guarding mutations\", says what each action checks before it writes. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rc-git-highlight","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is a pure tree-sitter wrapper the FFI exposes for the file pane: highlight spans, and the import links of a JavaScript or TypeScript file.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"The change list and sync","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"ChangesModel","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (RcGitKit) holds the Changes tab: the flat change list, one file's worktree diff, the stash list and the tick state that becomes a commit or stash selection. It only reads. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"WorktreeWatcher","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" decides which filesystem events can change the list and drops the rest; what remains marks the list stale. Scans coalesce: a request made while one runs marks it pending and returns, and the running scan re-reads once when it lands, so a burst of events costs one scan in flight plus one queued.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Writes go the other way. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"SyncModel","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (RcGitKit) runs the sync workflow — preflight, fetch, fast-forward pull, push — through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"RepositoryGuard","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which calls the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rcgit_guard_*","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" functions; each network step carries a ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"CancelToken","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" around an ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"RcGitCancel","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" handle, the only way to stop a thread blocked inside a transfer. The window controller runs the other guarded actions the same way and refreshes the change list afterwards.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Opening a repository","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Repository::open","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" calls ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"gix::ThreadSafeRepository::open_opts","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Options::isolated()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which reads only the repository's own ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"config","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". It then builds a small pool of ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"gix::Repository","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" handles, one per core up to four, each with a 32 MiB object cache and a 32 MiB pack delta-base cache, so an open repository holds at most 4 × (32 + 32) = 256 MiB in them. Both are set on every handle after the open, so the repository's own ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"gitoxide.objects.cacheLimit","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"core.deltaBaseCacheLimit","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" cannot raise or remove them. Every operation borrows a free handle through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Repository::with","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"; when all are busy a temporary handle is built so no call waits on another. A handle is single-threaded; the pool is what makes ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Repository","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Send + Sync","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Opening costs a few reads: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"HEAD","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"config","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", the pack index headers. Packs are memory-mapped on demand.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Selecting a ref","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"BrowserModel.attach","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" loads ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"refs()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"head()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" off the main actor. A repository with a working directory and a born ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"HEAD","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" opens on the working tree through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"selectWorkingTree","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"; otherwise ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"attach","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" picks the branch ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"HEAD","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is on and calls ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"select","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"select","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" resolves the ref's target to a tree id with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"treeOf","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and publishes ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rootTree","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". That is the whole cost of switching branches: one object read. Cached subtrees stay valid because they are keyed by tree id, not by branch.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Expanding a folder","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The tree view asks ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"BrowserModel.children(of:)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" for the folder's tree id. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"TreeStore","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" answers from its dictionary when it can; otherwise ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"treeEntries","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" decodes exactly that one tree object, sorts it for display (directories first, names ASCII-case-insensitive), stores it, and returns. Nothing below that folder is touched.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Opening a file","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"openFile","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" bumps the file generation, publishes ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".loading","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", and calls ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"readBlob","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" with a size limit. The core reads the object header first; anything above the limit returns ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"tooLarge","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" without decoding. Otherwise the blob is inflated, checked for a NUL in its first 8000 bytes (git's own binary rule), and, when text, indexed with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"memchr","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" for line starts and validated as UTF-8 — once, here, so no display layer re-scans the bytes. The result is applied only if the generation still matches.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Still off the main actor, the bytes decode as UTF-8 with replacement into a ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"TextDocument","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" carrying UTF-16 line starts. The file pane builds the attributed string in the background too, sets it on a TextKit 1 text storage with non-contiguous layout, and draws line numbers for visible fragments from the precomputed starts. Syntax colors arrive later as temporary attributes for the visible chunk only; scrolling colors further chunks. Markdown files can render as a styled preview instead, toggled from the file pane header: ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"MarkdownDocument","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (RcGitKit) parses the source into flat blocks and styled runs, and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"MarkdownRenderer","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (RcGitApp) turns those into the attributed string, wrapped, with the ruler hidden. Both halves are pure, so the preview is built off the main actor like the plain paint is. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"MarkdownLinkTarget","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" resolves what a link means — a URL, a repository path, or a heading — and is what the pane, its context menu, and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"BrowserModel.openPath","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" all agree on.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Source mode has links of its own in JavaScript and TypeScript. The first pointer move over a file asks ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"BrowserModel.importLinks","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" for them; ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ImportLinkMap","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" answers which one the pointer is on, and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"LinkTextView","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" underlines it without touching the text storage. A click hands the specifier to ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"BrowserModel.openImport","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", where ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"ImportResolver","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" reads the directories and config files it needs off the main actor and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"openPath","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" opens what it found.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Going back","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"For every move a tab makes, ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"BrowserModel","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" fires ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"onLocationChanged","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" once. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"location","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" names the tree browsed (the working tree, a ref by name, or one commit), the open file's path, the history scope, and the commit in the detail. A move that changes several of those reports after the last one — a ref switch also closes the open file — so the step in between is never recorded. The window controller adds the repository path and the pane to make a stop, and the app delegate records it in one ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"BackForwardList","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" for every tab, from the tab in front only.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Stepping back selects the stop's tab and calls ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"BrowserModel.restore","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which compares the stop with where the browser is and redoes only what differs: between two files of one tree that is one blob read. Restores coalesce the way the change list's scans do. One asked for while another runs replaces the pending location and returns; the running one stops at its next step and goes on to it. What a tab reports during a restore is not recorded.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Threading","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"BrowserModel","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"@MainActor","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". All state changes and callbacks happen there.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Repository calls, keychain reads and transfers run through ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"BlockingWork.run","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which runs them on a dedicated overcommitting dispatch queue and resumes the caller through a continuation. A blocking call on the cooperative pool (inside ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Task.detached","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") holds one of its few threads, and enough of them starve every task. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Repository","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"@unchecked Sendable","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"; the Rust side guarantees thread safety through the handle pool.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Every load carries a generation number captured before the await and compared after.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Caching","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
